Since $\bV[{ \beta }]$ is a $(\uqpg, R^J({ \beta }))$-bimodule, we can construct the following functor:
\begin{align}
\F_{ \beta } \colon \Modg(R^J(\beta)) &\rightarrow \Mod(\uqpg)\label{eq:the functor}
\end{align}
  sending an $R^J(\beta)$-module $M$  to the $\uqpg$-module
\eqn \F_{ \beta } (M) \seteq \bV[{ \beta }] \otimes_{R^J({ \beta })}
M. \eneqn
Set \eqn && \F_n \seteq \bigoplus_{\beta \in \rootl^+, \,
|\beta|=n } \F_\beta : \Mod(R^J(n))
\to \Mod(\uqpg),  \\
&& \F\seteq \soplus_{n\in\Z_{\ge0}}\F_n
\col\soplus_{n\in\Z_{\ge0}} \Mod(R^J(n)) \rightarrow \Mod(\uqpg).
\eneqn
